// spec: an argument whose class converts to the parameter by two equally good operators keeps the overload viable (C++ [over.best.ics]: an ambiguous conversion sequence is a user-defined one), and the call that chooses it is an error, never a silent choice of another overload
// error: ambiguous_conversion_keeps_overload_viable.kpp:13: error: the conversion of X to int32 is ambiguous: more than one of its conversion operators converts to it equally well
// factorio: D's review of 1514538a (overload ranking by the one conversion rule, design.md 24)
struct X
{
  implicit operator long long() const { return 1; }
  implicit operator long double() const { return 2; }
};
void f(int v) { std::println("int ", v); }
int main()
{
  X x;
  f(x);
  return 0;
}
